{"full":"hf:HumeAI/voice-replication-leaderboard","spaceId":"HumeAI/voice-replication-leaderboard","name":"Voice Replication Leaderboard","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":10,"created":"2026-08-28T23:57:21.000Z","updated":"2026-09-23T15:41:03.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://humeai-voice-replication-leaderboard.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/HumeAI/voice-replication-leaderboard","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T18:39:40.589Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T18:39:40.589Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T18:39:40.589Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🧬","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["How well text-to-speech models reproduce a specific person's voice from a short reference recording, rated by paid blind human raters.","Thirteen models replicate the same 25 reference voices across 7 delivery-neutral prompts, three raters per clip. One board tab, introduced by a short blurb above the table, with four subtabs: Overall first, then the three reference types (Standard, Emotional, Accent). Every subtab carries the same four columns, so the categories compare like with like.","sits to the reference's, 0 to 1. An automatic check on the human ratings. The footnote under the table names the model (TitaNet). It is not a probability and not a percentage, so the column carries no unit."],"features":["Same speaker (the ranking column): does the output sound like the","Quality: audio quality, independent of the match","Naturalness: how human the delivery sounds","Objective speaker similarity: how close the output's speaker embedding"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/HumeAI/voice-replication-leaderboard/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"96203a5200a4e1c51502618b2cdbe5a838868e3e263ec9a28cf6a8cb6